.Sh DESCRIPTION
An image source is the object
.Xr execve 2
activates: the thing whose header is read, whose segments are mapped,
whose permissions and set-id bits are checked, and which becomes the
process's text when the exec commits.
The exec core
.Pq Fn do_execve , the image activators, Fn exec_fail_dealloc
reaches it only through the operations table
.Va imgp->is_ops ,
a
.Vt "struct image_source_ops" ,
installed by the source's constructor together with the source's private
state in
.Va imgp->is_data .
The core never names a vnode: every vnode operation that used to be inline
lives in the vnode backend,
.Pa sys/kern/exec_image_vnode.c ,
in the order it used to run.
A served image, whose bytes come from a userland controller, is another
backend with no vnode at all.
.Pp
.Va imgp->is_ops
is
.Dv NULL
until a constructor has succeeded; that is the discriminator the core uses
for
.Dq a source exists and must be closed .
.Ss Constructors
The core builds the source from the three entry forms of
.Xr execve 2 :
.Bl -tag -width "IS_FORM_INTERP_LOADER"
.It Dv IS_FORM_PATH
.Fn exec_image_vnode_from_namei :
the path in
.Va args->fname
was looked up with
.Dv LOCKLEAF | LOCKSHARED | WANTPARENT ;
the source takes the vnode, its parent and the last component, which
become
.Va p_textvp , p_textdvp
and
.Va p_binname
when the exec commits.
.It Dv IS_FORM_INTERP_VNODE
.Fn exec_image_vnode_from_vnode :
an image activator
.Pq binmisc
handed over a referenced, unlocked interpreter vnode in
.Va imgp->interpreter_vp .
.It Dv IS_FORM_FD
.Fn exec_image_vnode_from_vnode :
.Xr fexecve 2 ;
the descriptor's vnode, referenced and unlocked.
.It Dv IS_FORM_INTERP_LOADER
.Fn exec_image_vnode_init :
the ELF interpreter loader built its own kernel-origin lookup and
constructs a source over the locked vnode; that source is never installed.
.El
.Pp
For the two
.Fn exec_image_vnode_from_vnode
forms the constructor resolves the path, locks the vnode and records the
audit argument itself, because
.Dv AUDIT_ARG_VNODE1
needs the locked vnode and cannot be emitted by a vnode-free core.
.Ss Operations
The image is locked for
.Fn IS_CHECK ,
.Fn IS_READ ,
every
.Fn IS_MAC
phase,
.Fn IS_AUTHORITY_PREPARE ,
.Fn IS_INSTALL
and
.Fn IS_ACCESSED ;
the
.Dv IS_MAC_TRANSITION
and
.Dv IS_MAC_RELABEL
phases also run under the process lock and must not sleep.
.Bl -tag -width "IS_AUTHORITY_PREPARE"
.It Fn IS_LOCK , Fn IS_UNLOCK , Fn IS_ASSERT_LOCKED
The source's lock.
The core unlocks around operations that may sleep
.Pq Fn crdup , Fn uifind , Fn malloc "M_WAITOK" , Fn copyout , the hwpmc and HWT hooks
and relocks, as it always did with the vnode; the vnode backend takes the
lock shared, a source without a lock does nothing.
.It Fn IS_CHECK
.Fn exec_check_permissions :
fill
.Va imgp->attr ,
run the MAC exec check, refuse
.Dv MNT_NOEXEC ,
a non-executable mode, anything but a regular file and an empty file,
check
.Dv VEXEC ,
take the text reference
.Pq Va imgp->textset , Er ETXTBSY
and open the file
.Pq Va imgp->opened .
.It Fn IS_FIRST_PAGE
Reference the image's VM object into
.Va imgp->object
and map its first page
.Pq Va imgp->image_header .
.Fn exec_unmap_first_page
and the object's release stay in the core.
.It Fn IS_READ
Read
.Fa len
bytes at
.Fa off
beyond the first page
.Pq program headers, Dv PT_INTERP , Dv PT_NOTE .
.It Fn IS_MAP_COW , Fn IS_MAP_TEXT
The extra
.Dv MAP_*
flags a mapping of the image takes
.Pq Dv MAP_VN_EXEC
and the per-mapping text reference taken after a successful mapping.
A source without text references returns 0 and does nothing.
.It Fn IS_UNSET_TEXT
Drop the text reference
.Fn IS_CHECK
took, if it is still held.
.It Fn IS_PATH , Fn IS_COMMNAME
The image's path
.Pq for Va imgp->execpath
and the name for
.Va p_comm .
For the path form the path is resolved through the parent and the last
component; a lookup that produced no parent leaves the path unresolved,
as before.
.It Fn IS_NOSUID
Whether set-id bits and software authority are to be ignored
.Pq Dv MNT_NOSUID .
.It Fn IS_MAC
The MAC phases of the exec, in order:
.Dv IS_MAC_WILL_TRANSITION ,
.Dv IS_MAC_WILL_RELABEL
.Pq return the hook's answer ,
.Dv IS_MAC_TRANSITION ,
.Dv IS_MAC_RELABEL ,
and
.Dv IS_MAC_INTERP_ENTER
when a
.Ql #!
script hands over to its interpreter
.Pq the label copy .
The vnode backend calls the
.Fn mac_vnode_execve_*
hooks.
.It Fn IS_AUTHORITY_PREPARE , Fn IS_AUTHORITY_EXEC
Software authority matching
.Pq Fn cap_authority_exec_prepare , Fn cap_authority_exec .
.Fn IS_AUTHORITY_EXEC
must be called by every backend: besides matching, it invalidates authority
held across the exec.
.It Fn IS_INSTALL , Fn IS_RELEASE_OLD
Install the image as the process's
.Pq Va p_textvp , p_textdvp , p_binname , p_image
under the process lock, saving what it displaced in
.Vt "struct image_source_old" ;
release the displaced state after the process and image locks are gone,
through the ops saved at install, since
.Fn IS_CLOSE
has by then cleared
.Va imgp->is_ops .
The displaced state may be another kind of image: the structure carries a
vnode triple and a file reference with its presented path.
.It Fn IS_ACCESSED
The image was executed
.Pq Dv VOP_UPDATE_ATIME .
.It Fn IS_CLOSE
Close the source: undo the open, drop the text reference, and either drop
the reference
.Pq Fa release ,
on an error or for a source that was never installed, or merely unlock it,
the reference now belonging to the process.
Frees
.Va imgp->is_data
and clears
.Va imgp->is_ops .
.El
.Sh DTRACE
.Bl -tag -width "proc:::exec-image-close"
.It proc:::exec-image-open
A source was constructed;
.Fa arg0
is the
.Vt "struct image_params *" ,
.Fa arg1
the
.Dv IS_FORM_*
form.
.It proc:::exec-image-close
A source was closed;
.Fa arg1
is non-zero when its reference was dropped.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr execve 2 ,
.Xr fexecve 2 ,
.Xr fileops 9 ,
.Xr mac 9 ,
.Xr vnode 9
.Sh HISTORY
The image source first appeared in 5BSD, as stage 0 of the DescriptorQueue
design, so that a process may execute an image that is not a vnode.
